        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThis is a result of `open` animation which shows which window was just opened. By default it does so by covering whole window with floating window which changes its 'winblend' option from being slightly opaque to completely transparent.\r\n\r\nAs your `NormalFloat` highlight group seems to already be \"transparent\" (i.e. no actual color as resolved background), Neovim seems to resort to black background.\r\n\r\nIn your case of transparent floating windows having `open` and `close` animations is kind of unusable at the moment, so disabling them should fix this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.animate').setup({\r\n  open = { enable = false },\r\n  close = { enable = false },\r\n})\r\n```",
